Subject: [PATCH] ARM: extend the module address space

These vendor trees reserve 20 MiB below PAGE_OFFSET for modules, and larger
WiFi modules fail to load once that area is used up. Reserve 23 MiB instead.

TASK_SIZE has to stay at or below the new MODULES_VADDR. A module at
MODULES_VADDR has to reach the end of the kernel text with a 32 MiB branch,
so the kernel text must stay below 9 MiB.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [machine-specific address-space layout]

diff -uNr a/arch/arm/include/asm/memory.h b/arch/arm/include/asm/memory.h
--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/memory.h	2018-08-01 11:13:19.000000000 +0800
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/memory.h	2022-11-07 17:33:40.488610900 +0800
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
  * and PAGE_OFFSET - it must be within 32MB of the kernel text.
  */
 #ifndef CONFIG_THUMB2_KERNEL
-#define MODULES_VADDR		(PAGE_OFFSET - 20*1024*1024)
+#define MODULES_VADDR		(PAGE_OFFSET - 23*1024*1024)
 #else
 /* smaller range for Thumb-2 symbols relocation (2^24)*/
 #define MODULES_VADDR		(PAGE_OFFSET - SZ_8M)
